<body>
    <h1>Meeting Minutes of 2026/06/22 - Plan Sharing</h1>
    <div class=3D"Section1">
        <p local-id=3D"8e63fc784846">Hi all,</p>
<p local-id=3D"9164403326d6">Thank you all for attending this meeting. Belo=
w are the meeting minutes and future work arrangements.</p>
<h2 local-id=3D"77bdb1645284" id=3D"MeetingMinutesof2026/06/22-PlanSharing-=
QuickRecap">Quick Recap</h2>
<p local-id=3D"13e9b70afd84">The meeting focused on the current project pro=
gress and next steps. Tao confirmed that the client demonstration would tak=
e place on July 17 and that an internal rehearsal would be held on July 6.<=
/p>
<p local-id=3D"df2a985c9e3b">Team members reported progress across differen=
t layers. Liu Huifang presented the technical architecture of KAG, or Knowl=
edge-Augmented Generation, including the Builder, reasoning engine, and kno=
wledge indexing components. Xie Daijiang reported that the Agent layer had =
completed integration with the actual tools, including retrieval result sta=
ndardization and end-to-end workflow integration. Mu Guangyuan completed th=
e JSON storage functions for the data processing pipeline. Dai Jiaxing impl=
emented vector retrieval, BM25 keyword retrieval, and hybrid retrieval. Son=
g Suijie completed the basic framework of the front-end interface.</p>
<p local-id=3D"db50f03b5764">The meeting concluded with a discussion on cod=
e collaboration standards. All team members are required to create their ow=
n branches and upload their code to the Git repository.</p>
<h2 local-id=3D"a492024b74a1" id=3D"MeetingMinutesof2026/06/22-PlanSharing-=
NextSteps">Next Steps</h2>
<h3 local-id=3D"00771706d446" id=3D"MeetingMinutesof2026/06/22-PlanSharing-=
Tao">Tao</h3>
<ul local-id=3D"c1fc75da-e510-4e5c-832e-9c06fd58fcff">
<li local-id=3D"d118d21b-c21d-4a6d-9e42-d3a505b2c54d">
<p local-id=3D"56a9184a049a">Organize and host the internal rehearsal for t=
he July 17 CPE results presentation during the weekly meeting on July 6.</p=
></li>
<li local-id=3D"0ba0eea1-caad-433d-8129-fa69eebbb0b1">
<p local-id=3D"b8795d6d96db">If Tao is unable to attend the rehearsal on Ju=
ly 6, Loura will assist in organizing and hosting it.</p></li>
</ul>
<h3 local-id=3D"f375d98122f2" id=3D"MeetingMinutesof2026/06/22-PlanSharing-=
Vincent">Vincent</h3>
<ul local-id=3D"ee9b18be-b1ed-4c6f-82d2-180665652fd9">
<li local-id=3D"caa5807b-7de6-4952-93d2-b778a2365b76">
<p local-id=3D"30bcba62d60c">Conduct a second rehearsal around July 13 and =
provide final adjustments to the presentation.</p></li>
</ul>
<h3 local-id=3D"9d95986efa4e" id=3D"MeetingMinutesof2026/06/22-PlanSharing-=
LiuHuifang">Liu Huifang</h3>
<ul local-id=3D"dc9c90b4-751c-4386-a773-e4651d158758">
<li local-id=3D"cc2cb3d1-6825-45e4-9ab0-35f179640d26">
<p local-id=3D"7f35575766c4">Continue searching for comparative experiments=
 or results on the accuracy and efficiency of KAG versus traditional knowle=
dge graph triples.</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"c35038ab-6435-4da2-bcfd-a16541acc87b">
<p local-id=3D"27183e3ba7b2">If no public results are available, consider r=
eproducing the idea and evaluating whether it provides measurable performan=
ce improvements.</p></li>
</ul>
<h3 local-id=3D"6a5774cc46bf" id=3D"MeetingMinutesof2026/06/22-PlanSharing-=
SongSuijie">Song Suijie</h3>
<ul local-id=3D"c31d7935-b629-4ef3-ac98-1f5de7acdafb">
<li local-id=3D"6896783c-1f49-428c-9167-e863e507f1f6">
<p local-id=3D"3b464b694dd9">Continue improving the front-end and back-end =
framework of the user layer.</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"8fee635c-d5dd-4b73-ad41-e9d3d1d469c7">
<p local-id=3D"6c48b5f1a964">Complete integration once the Agent layer is r=
eady.</p></li>
</ul>
<h3 local-id=3D"1ec6c872b390" id=3D"MeetingMinutesof2026/06/22-PlanSharing-=
DaiJiaxing">Dai Jiaxing</h3>
<ul local-id=3D"9d91d8e2-193a-4105-9308-d117a0df0a16">
<li local-id=3D"25ff9a53-7c74-4db5-beac-d8d3ee5eda0b">
<p local-id=3D"e0bb16538a63">Improve the presentation of the retrieval demo=
 for the tool layer.</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"6b3195ad-4c8b-41d6-8c9f-988bf29e388b">
<p local-id=3D"13d847acd4fb">Clearly highlight the key observations, result=
s, and conclusions.</p></li>
</ul>
<h3 local-id=3D"3c3d68c9b9d3" id=3D"MeetingMinutesof2026/06/22-PlanSharing-=
MuGuangyuan">Mu Guangyuan</h3>
<ul local-id=3D"fed9f8b2-7dc5-438f-97ca-f7d9a0f13cbe">
<li local-id=3D"e7679428-3551-4d0c-8f9d-971508285112">
<p local-id=3D"f21d7c527cd1">Continue supporting the integration between th=
e data processing pipeline and the tool layer according to the existing pla=
n.</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"bc539492-530e-4bf6-93be-644ee51f1d40">
<p local-id=3D"f212af752b5a">Ensure that subsequent retrieval calls can be =
completed successfully.</p></li>
</ul>
<h3 local-id=3D"0b7677f20fae" id=3D"MeetingMinutesof2026/06/22-PlanSharing-=
CollaborationRequirements">Collaboration Requirements</h3>
<ul local-id=3D"5cff8d58-aae2-421e-ac14-77d045c5add8">
<li local-id=3D"f691fb00-3a7a-4d8f-9aaf-4c96aeb2b84e">
<p local-id=3D"7e46b40de839"><strong>All team leaders:</strong> Update proj=
ect progress and technical documentation for their respective teams on Conf=
luence every week, clearly stating completed work and next steps.</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"c0c6f0de-6d97-4cbf-92e4-3a7ed335149c">
<p local-id=3D"17758819bd2f"><strong>All team members:</strong> Prepare a s=
hort demo or progress update each week to present completed work and issues=
 encountered.</p></li>
</ul>
<h2 local-id=3D"7ce8cd04981e" id=3D"MeetingMinutesof2026/06/22-PlanSharing-=
MeetingSummary">Meeting Summary</h2>
<h3 local-id=3D"5548315baa24" id=3D"MeetingMinutesof2026/06/22-PlanSharing-=
ConfirmationoftheJulyClientDemonstration">Confirmation of the July Client D=
emonstration</h3>
<p local-id=3D"9e13a4713bb8">Tao confirmed that the client demonstration wo=
uld take place on July 17. The proposed format includes a 10-minute PowerPo=
int presentation covering the project background and proposed solution, fol=
lowed by a 5-minute Q&amp;A session.</p>
<p local-id=3D"bcc7e373d672">Vincent suggested adjusting the preparation se=
quence by completing the working demo first and then preparing the PowerPoi=
nt materials. The team also discussed the July examination schedule. Mu Gua=
ngyuan stated that his examinations would continue until July 14. Tao propo=
sed completing the main materials by July 10 and conducting internal rehear=
sals in advance.</p>
<h3 local-id=3D"01773c9b5c14" id=3D"MeetingMinutesof2026/06/22-PlanSharing-=
ProjectScheduleDiscussion">Project Schedule Discussion</h3>
<p local-id=3D"a02750b0ce72">The team discussed the overall project schedul=
e and expected the main development work to be completed by July 4, leaving=
 approximately one week for integration and presentation preparation.</p>
<p local-id=3D"1ff4c9db9cd7">The team agreed to conduct the first rehearsal=
 during the weekly meeting on July 6. Vincent may be unable to attend the c=
lient meeting on July 17 because he may be on leave that week.</p>
<p local-id=3D"9c3f20a1dc48">At the end of the discussion, Liu Huifang enco=
untered a screen-sharing issue and required technical assistance.</p>
<h3 local-id=3D"fd18a0eaf316" id=3D"MeetingMinutesof2026/06/22-PlanSharing-=
KAGTechnicalArchitecturePresentation">KAG Technical Architecture Presentati=
on</h3>
<p local-id=3D"a0a83e8cc94b">Liu Huifang presented the technical architectu=
re of KAG, or Knowledge-Augmented Generation. The presentation focused on c=
omponents such as the Builder, knowledge representation, knowledge indexing=
, and reasoning engine.</p>
<p local-id=3D"073049f31b0c">The architecture was discussed at two main lev=
els:</p>
<ul local-id=3D"4b3a49f8-e7ed-4191-bc74-c11a19d4e31a">
<li local-id=3D"c8349b2b-3d02-4d36-82b4-d0935963e11e">
<p local-id=3D"5f0668819345">Knowledge indexing and offline knowledge const=
ruction</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"0e03c094-2b23-4d58-88f2-357cb50451ad">
<p local-id=3D"4679009b46c8">Online reasoning and retrieval</p></li>
</ul>
<p local-id=3D"0cdc02d939e3">The online reasoning system includes a hybrid =
reasoning engine guided by logical forms, together with semantic reasoning =
capabilities.</p>
<p local-id=3D"9a7c96cb02e9">Wang Yixi helped Liu Huifang resolve the scree=
n-sharing issue. Liu Huifang then invited the team to raise questions and d=
iscuss the technical approach.</p>
<h3 local-id=3D"496354a8a627" id=3D"MeetingMinutesof2026/06/22-PlanSharing-=
DiscussiononTripleandStructuredRepresentationConversion">Discussion on Trip=
le and Structured Representation Conversion</h3>
<p local-id=3D"612217cf49b9">Tao asked whether KAG had compared traditional=
 knowledge graph triples with JSON-like structured representations or embed=
ding-based representations, particularly in terms of performance and accura=
cy.</p>
<p local-id=3D"4ced8f59b0a3">Liu Huifang suggested that the structured repr=
esentation approach might improve performance because knowledge is organize=
d into a model-friendly format during the initial processing stage.</p>
<p local-id=3D"4d65d65a1c66">Vincent asked whether this LLM-friendly format=
 was fixed. Liu Huifang explained that it could be customized by users. She=
 also noted that knowledge types could be divided into three layers to supp=
ort more domain-specific and personalized representations.</p>
<p local-id=3D"c64cd5fba18a">Mu Guangyuan asked about the purpose of confid=
ence scores and the three knowledge layers. Liu Huifang explained that they=
 could support knowledge extraction accuracy and help large language models=
 understand composite entities and relationships.</p>
<h3 local-id=3D"6e73e1203da5" id=3D"MeetingMinutesof2026/06/22-PlanSharing-=
SystemArchitectureandConfidenceScoreCalculation">System Architecture and Co=
nfidence Score Calculation</h3>
<p local-id=3D"b52068be34e8">Liu Huifang explained the design principles of=
 the rigorous layer, flexible layer, and domain layer within the system arc=
hitecture.</p>
<p local-id=3D"c5dfff2e7b59">Mu Guangyuan asked how confidence scores shoul=
d be calculated. Liu Huifang stated that confidence scores should preferabl=
y be defined and calculated by the structured knowledge base or system desi=
gner to avoid introducing additional uncertainty.</p>
<p local-id=3D"dbb66644ff2c">Vincent added that the meaning and calculation=
 of confidence scores depend on the specific standards, scenarios, and inte=
nded applications.</p>
<p local-id=3D"3a944b37785b">Liu Huifang also reported the progress of the =
Agent layer. The basic architecture and local implementation of the tool-le=
vel interface had been completed, together with initial retrieval pipeline =
testing. The team planned to begin integration with the actual tools for fu=
rther testing in the following week.</p>
<h3 local-id=3D"e5782f151ccf" id=3D"MeetingMinutesof2026/06/22-PlanSharing-=
AgentLayerWeek2Progress">Agent Layer Week 2 Progress</h3>
<p local-id=3D"401d6ba9b741">Xie Daijiang reported the main progress of the=
 Agent layer during Week 2.</p>
<p local-id=3D"296b73f1e7bb">The team completed:</p>
<ul local-id=3D"0e13d97d-dba3-441a-804b-ff24ea34b67e">
<li local-id=3D"3115aa7b-de7f-49fc-ac38-f861b16606f3">
<p local-id=3D"5e077d8ab0e6">Integration with the actual tool layer</p></li=
>
<li local-id=3D"b18a3074-24f7-418c-80c1-f4120bcb189a">
<p local-id=3D"8035075315d1">Tool invocation</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"f5ffa707-df0e-4c2e-86cd-f3b99568559b">
<p local-id=3D"0a15b38c2d58">Retrieval result standardization</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"94b176ff-8579-45de-9a60-04a1ac695189">
<p local-id=3D"ee63d465c3a0">End-to-end integration of the main workflow</p=
></li>
<li local-id=3D"0c9e3254-1a6b-474b-ad0c-a68b303cc880">
<p local-id=3D"8a321ee52e25">Smoke testing of the retrieval pipeline</p></l=
i>
</ul>
<p local-id=3D"478194780d14">The team also discussed the need to prepare we=
ekly technical documentation and demos.</p>
<p local-id=3D"b9a4c5afec7b">Vincent emphasized that effective presentation=
 and demonstration skills are important. Each team should clearly explain w=
hat has been completed, what the demo is intended to show, and what conclus=
ions the audience should draw.</p>
<p local-id=3D"ee12641228f1">Mu Guangyuan then reported progress on the dat=
a processing pipeline. The JSON storage and related processing functions ha=
d been completed. The relevant code and API documentation were uploaded to =
Git and shared with the team.</p>
<h3 local-id=3D"440676fe3db8" id=3D"MeetingMinutesof2026/06/22-PlanSharing-=
DataPersistenceandRetrievalInterfaceDevelopment">Data Persistence and Retri=
eval Interface Development</h3>
<p local-id=3D"c40e652fc7b7">Wang Yixi confirmed that the relevant call and=
 interface-related work had been completed.</p>
<p local-id=3D"71a88e00ddda">Mu Guangyuan stated that the retrieval interfa=
ce required by the tool layer should also have been completed.</p>
<p local-id=3D"ec69ce6fa49a">Wang Yixi reported on the data persistence lay=
er, noting that the basic work had already been completed and demonstrated =
during the previous week, with no major new updates during the current week=
.</p>
<p local-id=3D"102c0a1682dd">Dai Jiaxing introduced the work completed duri=
ng the week, including the implementation of vector retrieval and RRF-based=
 fusion. He also demonstrated a simple retrieval example involving requirem=
ents for a web chat page and document filtering functions.</p>
<h3 local-id=3D"acdbdda4b1f4" id=3D"MeetingMinutesof2026/06/22-PlanSharing-=
HybridRetrievalSystemDemonstration">Hybrid Retrieval System Demonstration</=
h3>
<p local-id=3D"342099192747">Dai Jiaxing demonstrated a hybrid retrieval sy=
stem combining vector retrieval and BM25 keyword retrieval. He explained ho=
w the system ranks relevant results according to retrieval scores.</p>
<p local-id=3D"2917d07678b7">Song Suijie then presented the reconstructed u=
ser-layer front-end interface. The basic functions included conversation na=
ming, recommended questions, and model switching.</p>
<p local-id=3D"ce756e26fc2c">Wang Yixi emphasized the code collaboration re=
quirements:</p>
<ul local-id=3D"ec0ad6ab-afa2-45a7-9e5b-1e922650d6d9">
<li local-id=3D"a2f4164f-f46d-487d-9030-8a6f5732bf1a">
<p local-id=3D"b1c3d18b88b2">Each developer should create and use an indivi=
dual branch.</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"b9d023b1-2b3b-4179-b801-669ccd0ce81b">
<p local-id=3D"548c4e3a2ff4">Code should be uploaded to the Git repository =
through the correct branch.</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"92af8a70-e361-4b37-a34d-0f459b297907">
<p local-id=3D"02cddb14d4e3">Members should only upload files related to th=
eir own layer.</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"036077f5-0a5d-4be8-b34c-cda592add415">
<p local-id=3D"e23d8823fa7e">Unrelated files should not be included in code=
 submissions.</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"3134f219-8f8a-4fdf-98b7-f8addec49369">
<p local-id=3D"8d5cf759036a">Repository files should remain clearly organiz=
ed.</p></li>
</ul>
<p local-id=3D"214f7f4cc531">Tao asked the team to provide reference templa=
tes for Confluence. Wang Yixi again reminded everyone to maintain proper fi=
le organization when submitting code.</p>
<p local-id=3D"b5850ff4279a"></p>
<p class=3D"media-group"><img height=3D"250" style=3D"margin: 2px; border: =
1px solid #ddd; box-sizing: border-box; vertical-align: text-bottom;" src=
=3D"ebb93b025d77f3c390f84fd29213a5ea43bfbd924cc09ff40e249895324850fc" width=
=3D"250"></p>
<p local-id=3D"c405bc5fde2a"></p>
    </div>
